.TH RATTSPEC 1 "2026-10-05" "Rattpack 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rattspec \- create or update Rattpack specifications using OpenCode
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rattspec assist
.I REQUEST
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rattspec assist
creates or updates the root Rattspec and Rattpkg files from a natural-language
request. Quote REQUEST when it contains spaces or shell metacharacters.
It requires OpenCode V2 and the matching opencode-assist native plugin.
.PP
The command reads existing root files and a bounded inventory of source paths,
sends them through the opencode api CLI to OpenCode's experimental generation
endpoint, and accepts complete replacement files in a JSON proposal.
Unchanged files can be omitted; missing root files must be created.
.PP
Before writing, the whole proposal must parse and lint, declare exactly one
project/package identity, and include at least one target in Rattspec.
The real package manifest reader validates dependency sources, pins, and
checksums. Generated Rattscript is never evaluated. Files are published
atomically only if their existing contents still match the initial read.
.PP
The command does not resolve dependencies or write Rattpkg.lock. Follow-up
steps may appear in the generated summary.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-C " DIRECTORY" ", \--directory=" DIRECTORY
Project directory. Default: current directory.
.TP
.BI \--plugin= PATH
Assist plugin library. Default: plugins/opencode-assist with the platform's
shared-library suffix, beside the rattspec executable. The plugin must match
the host's D compiler family/major and shared runtime.
.TP
.BI \--opencode= EXECUTABLE
OpenCode executable name or path. Default: opencode, found using PATH.
.TP
.BI \--server= URL
Explicit OpenCode server URL. By default, use the CLI's discovery and
authentication.
.TP
.BI \--model= MODEL
Select provider/model or provider/model#variant.
Default: OpenCode's configured model.
.TP
.BI \--timeout= SECONDS
IPC deadline. Default: 120 seconds. Must be a positive integer no larger than
2147483647.
.TP
.B \--dry-run
Generate and validate the proposal, print it as JSON, and write no files.
The OpenCode request still runs.
.TP
.B \-h, \--help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.B \--version
Display the version and exit.
.PP
Boolean long options accept negative spellings such as \--no-dry-run.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I Rattspec
Root project identity and build targets.
.TP
.I Rattpkg
Root package identity and dependencies.
.TP
.I PREFIX/bin/plugins/opencode-assist.so
Default plugin location on POSIX. macOS uses .dylib and Windows uses .dll.
Install the plugin using install.sh \--with-plugins, or select \--plugin.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PATH
Search path for the default OpenCode executable.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success, help, or version output; 1 indicates an application
diagnostic or assist failure; 2 indicates argument parsing failure.
Diagnostics go to standard error. E_ASSIST reports failed or timed-out requests,
invalid responses, and concurrent edits; E_PLUGIN_ABI reports plugin failures.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
rattspec assist 'add these libraries: fmt and zlib'
rattspec assist 'build a C library and an executable that links it' \-C workspace
rattspec assist 'make this a monorepo' \--dry-run
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rattbuild (1),
.BR rattpkg (1),
.BR rattsc (1)
